# robots.txt — crawler guidance for the GHPLS website
#
# IMPORTANT, honest note: robots.txt is a *request*, not a wall. Well-behaved
# search engines (Google, Bing) obey it. Malicious scrapers and many AI
# crawlers ignore it. Truly blocking bad bots requires a WAF, not this file.
# This file does the realistic, useful things: keep the admin panel out of
# search results and opt out of the major AI training crawlers.
#
# This is a template, not a static file, so the sitemap URL below is generated
# from site.url and cannot drift away from the domain the site is actually on.
# The previous static version pointed at a Netlify domain for months after the
# site moved to Cloudflare.

# Allow normal search engines to index the public pages.
User-agent: *
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin/

# NOTE: /assets/uploads/ is deliberately NOT disallowed.
#
# It used to be, and that was a mistake worth spelling out so nobody re-adds
# it: the build writes every responsive image variant to
# /assets/uploads/resized/, so disallowing the parent path blocked *every
# photograph on the site* from Google. The society's competition and event
# photos are a large part of why anyone shares these pages, and they were
# invisible to image search and unavailable for link previews the whole time.

# Opt out of common AI / LLM training scrapers (they honour these tokens).
User-agent: GPTBot
Disallow: /

User-agent: ClaudeBot
Disallow: /

User-agent: Claude-Web
Disallow: /

User-agent: Google-Extended
Disallow: /

User-agent: CCBot
Disallow: /

User-agent: anthropic-ai
Disallow: /

User-agent: PerplexityBot
Disallow: /

User-agent: Applebot-Extended
Disallow: /

